\title{auxiv: Auxiliary Instrumental Variable Estimation for Nonlinear Models}
\description{
Implements the Auxiliary Instrumental Variable (AIV) estimator of D'Adamo, Weidner and Windmeijer for non-linear models with endogenous covariates. The instruments are added to the model as auxiliary regressors and the structural coefficients are chosen so that the estimated auxiliary coefficients are close to zero. The estimator is consistent when the coefficients on the endogenous regressors are zero and is locally sign consistent, without imposing any functional form or distributional assumption on the first stage. Supports the binary choice (probit, logit, cloglog) and Poisson cases via the standard 'family' interface, and provides standard errors valid under over-identification. Also provides the Rivers-Vuong control function estimator for comparison, with standard errors that correct for estimation of the first stage and with a choice of normalisation of the structural error variance.
}
